
Generic WHDLoad KickEmu Starter by JOTD, Wepl

Can be used to run programs/demos/games using WHDLoad's kickstart
emulation. This may work with some programs if they are compatible enough.

Usage:

Copy the stuff you like to start into the data directory.
Use the option Custom to specify which executable should be started and which
arguments should be passed to it.

Example:

WHDLoad GenericKick13.slave PRELOAD CUSTOM="program argument1 argument2 etc..."

Or if you use an icon from the workbench:

SLAVE=GenericKick13.slave
PRELOAD
CUSTOM=madnessII

The sources are available at https://github.com/wepl/winstalls, so GenericKick
may be extended and you may also assemble other Slaves with different memory
settings.


History:

1.0 (08.12.2002) by JOTD
- initial release

1.1 (01.11.2007) by Wepl
- adapted for new kickemu and WHDLoad v16+
- keyboard fix in the Kickstart 1.3 slave removed because it is already in
  kickemu now

1.2 (24.04.2016) by Wepl
- better error handling
- caches disabled
- memory set to 1 MB/2 MB chip only for better compatibility
- reassembled with latest kickemu

1.3 (15.11.2021) by Wepl
- SetKeyboard, SegTracker, WHDCtrl enabled
- reassembled with latest kickemu

1.4 (03.10.2022) by Wepl
- reassembled with latest kickemu

1.5 (19.02.2023) by Wepl
- WHDCtrl for Kickstart 1.3 enabled

1.6 (09.12.2025) by Wepl
- assembled with latest kickemu sources
- sources available: https://github.com/wepl/winstalls

1.7 (11.07.2026) by Wepl
- fixed WHDCtrl which was only working with the A1200 kickstart, it is now
  available with the A600 and A4000 kickstart too

